From 95647b60e1d04fec16ec9fdf14a907be31fd175e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stefan <kloterstefan@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 07:36:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 17/19] Vizzbox 1.1: room for the live control: QUARK's own
 look left out (6 684 bytes)

BRIEF-VIZZBOX-1.1.md 7: the live control (its part A) does not fit in the 3 612 bytes above the 2 KB reserve. Skiff's
own pages, layers and browser do the work (step 1); the own code gives nothing back (step 2: noinline on the
producer's and the VIZZBOX's functions the compiler puts into ui_input.c and main.c makes the app 3 552 bytes larger,
on the three called from several places 48); the FM-1 build holds no SMK-37, debug or demo code to drop (step 3). Of
what a FM-1 notices least (step 4), the decorations of one look, the smallest of the three that is enough: QUARK's
detector display (the cells' bracket corners, dotted rules, nuclei, particle tracks, collisions: ui_quark.c and the
branches in the drawing code; NEON's 7 796 and CRYPT's 7 872 would be more). The QUARK palette stays, its colours
drawn as SKIFF's BLOCKS; CRYPT and NEON keep theirs; LARGE (3 548 bytes, the legibility of the values, a function)
and SHIFT's help stay. A build flag, FELUCCA_QUARK_UI=1, puts it back (gfx.c UX_QUARK for ux.quark in the drawing
code). tests/ui_golden.txt: the 712 QUARK pictures, no other; tests/vizzbox_ui_golden.txt: its one QUARK GROOVEBOX
screen; tests/ui_test.c: QUARK's playhead without its collision.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01R1rawochSWXFaES57pjc4r
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
